BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Children's Baking Workshop
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTSTAMP:20261107T163656Z
UID:334fe5d4697f26db79d45c436740@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:The Museum of Work and Culture's annual Children’s Baking Wo
 rkshop with Wright’s Dairy Farm &amp\; Bakery will be held on Saturday\,
  November 7 at 11am. This year’s event will feature an éclair-making de
 monstration with a pastry chef from Wright's and special behind-the-scenes
  footage from the farm. Follow along with the chef to fill and assemble yo
 ur pastry\, then join museum educators for an interactive French language 
 matching game and baking bingo. Each participant will receive a chef's hat
 \, apron\, recipe card\, pre-printed activity materials\, and éclair ingr
 edients. Tickets are $25 for one child and one adult. Tickets are an addit
 ional $18 for a second child. No more than two children per adult can be a
 ccommodated. Space is limited\, and early registration is strongly encoura
 ged. TICKETS\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/childrens-b
 aking-workshop/112497/
LOCATION:Museum of Work & Culture\, 42 South Main Street\, Woonsocket\, RI
  02895
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/childrens-baking-workshop/11249
 7/
END:VEVENT
